{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "יהיה לך", :translit "yihyeh lakh", :gloss "shall be to you"} {:he "ואל משה אמר", :translit "v'el mosheh amar", :gloss "and to Moses He said"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: reading the end of one verse as contiguous with the opening of the next"}], :frame {:text "Nadab and Abihu, along with the seventy elders, ascended Mount Sinai and beheld a vision of the God of Israel (Exodus 24:1, 9–11). At Sinai they ate and drank yet were not punished; but later they offered unauthorized fire and died (Leviticus 10:1–2). Ba'al HaTurim reads the proximity of the snare-warning to the passage introducing Nadab and Abihu as signalling that the very vision of the Shechinah they witnessed at Sinai became a deadly snare, culminating in their death.", :sources ["Exodus 24:1" "Exodus 24:9-11" "Leviticus 10:1-2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: reading the end of one verse as contiguous with the opening of the next", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:51.592513303Z", :model "glm-5.2"}